        {
          "id": "b7126977-121b-356c-a4e4-d48ff5bda222",
          "content": {
            "id": "b7126977-121b-356c-a4e4-d48ff5bda222",
            "contentType": "VIDEO",
            "title": "SpaceX seeks $800B val., theater stocks fall on Netflix news",
            "description": "<p>Yahoo Finance Senior Reporter <a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/author/brooke-dipalma/?fr=sycsrp_catchall\">Brooke DiPalma</a> joins Market Domination host <a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/author/josh-lipton/\">Josh Lipton</a> to discuss some of Friday's trending tickers and stories.</p>\n<p>Movie theater stocks, like AMC (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/AMC\">AMC</a>), iMax (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:4;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/IMAX\">IMAX</a>), and Cinemark (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:5;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/CNK\">CNK</a>), are moving lower after Netflix's (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:6;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/NFLX\">NFLX</a>) Warner Bros. (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:7;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/WBD\">WBD</a>) deal was announced.</p>\n<p>SpaceX (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:8;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/SPAX.PVT\">SPAX.PVT</a>) is reportedly in talks for $800 billion valuation via a share sale, <a data-i13n=\"cpos:9;pos:1\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/business/spacex-in-talks-for-share-sale-that-would-boost-valuation-to-800-billion-b2852191\">according to the Wall Street Journal</a>.</p>\n<p>Southwest Airlines (<a data-i13n=\"cpos:10;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/LUV\">LUV</a>) lowered its profit guidance for the full year, citing disruption from the government shutdown.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more <a data-i13n=\"cpos:11;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-domination/\">Market Domination</a>.</p>",
            "summary": "Yahoo Finance Senior Reporter Brooke DiPalma joins Market Domination host Josh Lipton to discuss some of Friday's trending tickers and stories. Movie theater stocks, like AMC (AMC), iMax (IMAX), and Cinemark (CNK), are moving lower after Netflix's (NFLX) Warner Bros. (WBD) deal was announced. SpaceX (SPAX.PVT) is reportedly in talks for $800 billion valuation via a share sale, according to the Wall Street Journal. Southwest Airlines (LUV) lowered its profit guidance for the full year, citing disruption from the government shutdown. To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more Market Domination.",
